  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Four cells, each of emf $E$ and internal resistance $r,$ are connected in series across an external resistance $R .$ By mistake one of the cells is connected in reverse. Then the current in the external circuit is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EKHnn",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 E}{4 r+R}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4m4Ld",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 E}{4 r+R}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UCydl",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 E}{3 r+R}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d9jjB",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 E}{3 r+R}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Total emf of the cell $=3 E-E=2 E$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_phy_a40.png\">\r\n\r\nTotal internal resistance $=4 r$\r\n$\\therefore$ Total resistance of the circuit $=4 r+R$ So, the current in the external circuit $\\left(\\because i=\\frac{V}{B}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$$\r\ni=\\frac{2 E}{4 r+R}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
